  "question": {
    "text": "Let the centre of a circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></math> &nbsp;and its radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></math> be two tangents and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> be a normal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>. Then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
